We were taken to a large room that was being used as the check-in area. My credit card was taken from me to be added to our reservation for incidental charges. The card was out of my possession for an extended period of time while we waited to be checked in. 
When we returned from our vacation on XX/XX/2023, I immediately checked my credit card account online. I discovered an unauthorized charge of {$1800.00} from a merchant named XXXX made on the day of our check-in, XX/XX/2023. Upon researching this merchant, it is listed as a taxi service. We did not use this service as we had our own private transportation from the airport through the resort. Logistically, the charge doesn't even make sense as we were not in the country long enough to have a taxi charge of this amount from the airport. XXXX XXXX is only about XXXX minutes. Once we arrived at the resort and checked in, we never left the resort until we checked out on XX/XX/2023. 
