7775600,2023-10-30,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"I am writing to formally dispute the reporting of late payments on my XXXX XXXX file, specifically related to XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX Upon reviewing my credit report ( Reference Number : XXXX ), I noticed that these late payments are inaccurately reported, which is adversely affecting my creditworthiness. 
Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act : 15 USC 1681 Section 602 guarantees my right to privacy. This ensures the confidentiality of my credit report and mandates that information on it must be reported in a way that is fair and accurate to protect the consumer 's privacy.

15 USC 1681 Section 604a Section 2 stipulates that a consumer reporting agency can not furnish a report containing information on a consumer 's credit worthiness, credit standing, credit capacity, character, general reputation, personal characteristics, or mode of living without the consumer 's written instructions.

In light of these provisions, I challenge the authenticity and validity of the late payments recorded on my account and request your agency to produce evidence or documentation that validates this reporting in accordance with my written instructions.

Moreover, in alignment with 15 USC 1666b, a creditor may not treat a payment on a credit card account under an open-end consumer credit plan as late for any purpose unless they have adopted reasonable procedures designed to ensure that each periodic statement contains the required information. Hence, I demand proof that the said procedures were correctly adhered to in my case If you can not produce the necessary documents validating these late payment entries, or if the entries are found to be inaccurate, I kindly demand that they be deleted immediately or be updated to reflect as Paid on Time or OK.

It is essential for credit reporting agencies to ensure that all consumer reports are accurate, and any inaccuracies are dealt with in a swift manner. I trust that you will handle this matter with the urgency and attention it demands. 
Please initiate an investigation into this matter immediately. According to the FCRA, you are required to conduct this investigation within 30 days of receiving this letter. Upon completion, I request to be informed of the outcome of your investigation and to receive an updated copy of my credit report if any corrections are made. 
I thank you in advance for your cooperation and expect a prompt resolution.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",NJ,08028,,Web,2023-10-30,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
